    "q-74908": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74908",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (-2,-2)}\\sqrt{xy}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt{xy}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous except when the expression under the radical   is negative. However, for the point $(-2,-2)$ the product $x\\cdot y$ is not negative, so we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(-2,-2)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-2,-2)}\\sqrt{xy}=\\sqrt{(-2)\\cdot (-2)}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
