xclass=\"ORD\"><munder><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></munder></mrow><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>4</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>However, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"157\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 32.008em;\"><mjx-table><mjx-itable><mjx-mtr><mjx-mtd style=\"text-align: right; padding-right: 0px; padding-bottom: 0.4em;\"><mjx-ms